<%#
Cistergraphia: Read (fol. 2r)
=============================

Purpose:
- Turns an SVG generated by this app back into its message

Design Decisions:
- A large drop zone first (drag, drop, or choose), pasting second
- Accepts either a file upload or pasted SVG code (upload wins when both are sent)
- A passphrase switches to secret mode decryption; a grille key reads a plate
  written under a grille (square: the decoder asks for the key without one)

- The scriptorium record: plates read on this browser, by rung, in one
  reserved line (counts only, kept in localStorage by app.js; nothing without it)

Constraints:
- Only SVGs generated by Cistergraphia can be decoded
- Posts to /decode endpoint
%>
<section class="leaf leaf--narrow" aria-labelledby="read-title">
  <p class="folio-mark" aria-hidden="true">fol. 2<sup>r</sup></p>
  <h1 id="read-title" class="rubric">Read a plate</h1>
  <p class="lede">Bring an image made here. Its signs are read back along its path, the snail or the turning rows; sealed ones need their passphrase, and those written under a grille need its key. A game plate opens as its puzzle, the reading desk, the bench or the board, with the decoder’s answer one click below.</p>
  <p class="record" data-record="read" aria-live="polite"></p>

  <form class="entry" method="post" action="/decode" enctype="multipart/form-data">
    <label class="dropzone" for="file" data-dropzone>
      <%== glyph_svg(9999, title: 'A Cistercian sign') %>
      <span class="dropzone-title">Drop an SVG here</span>
      <span class="dropzone-sub">or click to choose a file</span>
      <span class="dropzone-file" data-file-name aria-live="polite"></span>
      <input type="file" id="file" name="file" accept=".svg,image/svg+xml">
    </label>

    <details class="paste">
      <summary>…or paste its SVG code</summary>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="svg" class="visually-hidden">SVG code</label>
        <textarea id="svg" name="svg" rows="8" class="code" spellcheck="false"
                  placeholder="&lt;svg xmlns=&quot;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&quot; …"></textarea>
      </div>
    </details>

    <div class="field">
      <label for="passphrase">Passphrase <span class="label-note">· only for sealed images</span></label>
      <div class="passphrase">
        <input type="password" id="passphrase" name="passphrase" autocomplete="current-password"
               autocapitalize="off" spellcheck="false">
        <button type="button" class="btn btn--small" data-reveal="passphrase" aria-pressed="false">Show</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="field">
      <label for="grille">Grille key <span class="label-note">· only for plates written under a grille</span></label>
      <input type="text" id="grille" name="grille" class="key-input" placeholder="<%= Cistergraphia::Grille::EXAMPLE %>"
             autocomplete="off" autocapitalize="characters" spellcheck="false">
    </div>

    <button class="btn btn--primary" type="submit">Read</button>
  </form>
</section>
